---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Buying a Home in the Wichita Area | Charity Menefee"
  description="A patient, practical approach to buying a home in Wichita and nearby south-central Kansas communities."
>
  <div class="buying-page">
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="Buying roadmap"
      title="A clearer path from first questions to closing."
      intro="Buying a home involves a lot of decisions, but you don't have to think about all of them at once. Here's how the process typically unfolds and where I'll help along the way."
    />

    <section class="buying-roadmap-section" aria-label="Home-buying roadmap">
      <ol class="shell buying-roadmap">
        <li class="buying-stage" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body" aria-labelledby="buying-step-one-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">Before serious home shopping</p>
              <h2 id="buying-step-one-title">Get financially ready.</h2>
              <p>A lender can help you understand your loan options and what price range makes sense. The highest possible approval doesn't have to become your shopping target.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details">
              <p class="buying-list-intro">Consider the full monthly housing picture:</p>
              <ul class="buying-checklist">
                <li>Purchase price and expected loan payment</li>
                <li>Property taxes and homeowners insurance</li>
                <li>Association dues when they apply</li>
                <li>Utilities, upkeep, and room in your budget</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">I can keep the search aligned with your range while your lender handles financing advice.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage buying-stage-priorities" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body" aria-labelledby="buying-step-two-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">Before the listings take over</p>
              <h2 id="buying-step-two-title">Figure out what matters most.</h2>
              <p>A focused search starts with how you want to live and the tradeoffs you can accept. I'll help separate must-haves from preferences.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details">
              <ul class="buying-checklist buying-checklist-priorities">
                <li>Location and commute</li>
                <li>Home size and layout</li>
                <li>Lot, neighborhood, or acreage</li>
                <li>Age, condition, and maintenance</li>
                <li>Willingness to make updates</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">Around Wichita, that may mean comparing established neighborhoods, newer suburbs, nearby communities, or land. The <a href="/communities/">community guides</a> can help you get oriented.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage buying-stage-tour" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body" aria-labelledby="buying-step-three-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">Once serious showings begin</p>
              <h2 id="buying-step-three-title">Tour homes with a critical eye.</h2>
              <p>In-person visits show how the layout, lot, condition, and surroundings work together beyond the listing photos.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details buying-tour-callout">
              <p class="buying-list-intro">Look beyond the listing photos:</p>
              <ul class="buying-checklist">
                <li>How the layout feels from room to room</li>
                <li>Visible maintenance or condition concerns</li>
                <li>Lot characteristics and neighboring properties</li>
                <li>Items that deserve professional follow-up</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">I'll track observations and follow-up questions. Qualified professionals should evaluate the home's systems and condition.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage buying-stage-offer" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body" aria-labelledby="buying-step-four-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">When the right property appears</p>
              <h2 id="buying-step-four-title">Make an offer and do the homework.</h2>
              <p>An offer combines price, financing, timing, contingencies, and other terms. I'll explain the tradeoffs behind each choice.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details">
              <div class="buying-decision-grid">
                <section aria-labelledby="buying-offer-terms-title">
                  <h3 id="buying-offer-terms-title">Offer terms</h3>
                  <p>Look at the proposal as a whole, not only the headline price.</p>
                </section>
                <section aria-labelledby="buying-inspections-title">
                  <h3 id="buying-inspections-title">Inspections</h3>
                  <p>An accepted offer doesn't end the investigation. Qualified professionals may need to evaluate the property.</p>
                </section>
                <section aria-labelledby="buying-decisions-title">
                  <h3 id="buying-decisions-title">Decisions</h3>
                  <p>If inspections or other information bring up new questions, we'll go through them before you decide what to do next.</p>
                </section>
              </div>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">Specific document, legal, or financial questions should go to the appropriate professionals.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage buying-stage-closing" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body" aria-labelledby="buying-step-five-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">After acceptance</p>
              <h2 id="buying-step-five-title">Get from contract to closing.</h2>
              <p>The path can vary, but several pieces may still need to come together.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details">
              <ul class="buying-checklist buying-checklist-closing">
                <li>Lender coordination and appraisal, when applicable</li>
                <li>Title and closing work</li>
                <li>Contract items and final walkthrough</li>
                <li>Closing and transfer of ownership</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">I'll organize deadlines, coordinate with the people involved, and make sure you know which item needs attention.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <CallToAction
      title="Where are you in the process?"
      copy="Not sure where to start, or already looking at a particular home? Tell me what you're considering, and I'll help you figure out the next step."
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
